# Day 02 — TCP/IP Protocols, Ports & Network Services

## 🎯 Objective

Understand common network protocols, port numbers, client/server communication, listening ports, sockets, and why attackers perform port scanning.

---

## 📚 Topics Learned

### 1. TCP/IP Protocol Suite

TCP/IP is a collection of protocols used for communication between devices over networks.

Main layers:

* Application Layer — HTTP, HTTPS, DNS, SSH, SMTP
* Transport Layer — TCP, UDP
* Internet Layer — IP, ICMP
* Network Access Layer — Ethernet, Wi-Fi, ARP

---

### 2. Common Network Protocols

| Protocol | Purpose                         |     Common Port |
| -------- | ------------------------------- | --------------: |
| HTTP     | Web communication               |          TCP 80 |
| HTTPS    | Secure web communication        |         TCP 443 |
| DNS      | Domain name resolution          |      UDP/TCP 53 |
| DHCP     | Automatic network configuration |       UDP 67/68 |
| ARP      | IPv4-to-MAC resolution on LAN   | No TCP/UDP port |
| ICMP     | Network diagnostics/control     | No TCP/UDP port |
| FTP      | File transfer                   |          TCP 21 |
| SFTP     | Secure file transfer over SSH   |          TCP 22 |
| SSH      | Secure remote access            |          TCP 22 |
| SMTP     | Sending/relaying email          |          TCP 25 |
| POP3     | Email retrieval                 |         TCP 110 |
| IMAP     | Email access/synchronization    |         TCP 143 |

